A step-targeted rule never reaches the composed playbook section: with only a `{playbook}/{step}`
rule present and the step detached (fetch-form), the composed render carries no `## Rules` section
and no blank line where it would sit.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core: {namespace: fx, path: ~/core-specs}
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/rule/0002-step-rule.md --
---
type: rule
title: Step rule
status: accepted
targets: [fx-rule-step-only/s1]
brief: Step brief.
---
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-step-only/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-rule-step-only
title: Rules
summary: Rule injection.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-step-only/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  s1: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-step-only/s1/prompt.md --
---
name: s1
summary: Only step.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Step body.
